# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# Dependencies and build output, at any depth: pnpm gives every workspace
# package its own node_modules, and every app its own .next.
node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
coverage

# next.js
.next/
out/

# production
build/

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
!.env.example

# Local MVP store. Any json under any data/ directory, at any depth — the
# rule used to be root-anchored, and moving the app into apps/anon silently
# un-ignored the live store. A stale copy of it once held plaintext World ID
# nullifiers.
**/data/*.json

# Finder and cloud-sync duplicates ("name 2.ext"). Never intentional, and they
# carry whatever the original held at the time it was copied.
* [0-9].*

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Kept out of the public repo for now: the grant application, the launch
# blocker list, the build history and the design exports. They live on disk
# and are simply untracked — delete these four lines to publish them.
/GRANT.md
/SHIPPING.md
/WORKLOG.md
/design/
